"reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/9/#testresult/1cd0f04c41188d43","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793948341000,"stop":1793948735120,"duration":394120}},{"uid":"fa2b4b4f560db741","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/fa2b4b4f560db741","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793832981000,"stop":1793833399460,"duration":418460}},{"uid":"a86ac3948cda6c7d","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/6/#testresult/a86ac3948cda6c7d","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793657001000,"stop":1793657502260,"duration":501260}},{"uid":"db26b0c1dbda5c5e","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/5/#testresult/db26b0c1dbda5c5e","status":"failed","statusDetails":"timed out after 10m0.000367882s (excluding download) waiting for app \"dcb23eb6-e3f5-4bc4-8688-1a79c4a667cd\" (container-app) on device \"edge-dev\" to reach RUNNING state (last state: INSTALLED)\n\nClaude's conclusion:\nNo prior occurrence of this exact \"MOUNT-WEDGE-RECOVERY\" / stuck-mount signature in the ledger — this looks new. Found a clear root cause directly from live evidence.\n\n**Root cause:** The cdi-upload pod's PVC (`pvc-b47375af-...`) hit the kubelet volume-mount wedge that `zedkube`'s stuck-mount detector (`pkg/pillar/cmd/zedkube/stuckmount.go`, added 2026-08-31 in `092d7a326`) exists to catch: the volume attached successfully but kubelet never issued NodeStage, so the pod sat `Pending` indefinitely. The detector correctly identified this at `23:26:00.365` (\"`MOUNT-WEDGE-RECOVERY: restarting kubelet/k3s ... pod=cdi-upload-... Pending 5m43s`\") and restarted k3s to clear it, but by then the pod had already been wedged for ~6 minutes. The k3s restart itself knocked the apiserver out for ~21s (`connection refused` 23:26:00–23:26:21), and only after it came back did the `container-app` VMI actually get created (`SuccessfulCreate` ~23:27:29) — about 15 seconds *after* the test's 10-minute timeout had already fired at 23:27:14 (test started 22:57:51, app stuck at `INSTALLED` the whole time). So the app was never actually broken; it was just recovering one restart cycle too late relative to the test's fixed timeout.\n\nThis doesn't match any entry in `live-ledger.md` — no prior `TestSingleNodeCluster`/mount-wedge/CDI-upload-pending signature is recorded, and the wedge-recovery code itself is only ~2 months old, so this looks like a new (not previously recurring) failure mode: either the underlying kubelet mount-wedge bug this detector works around is occurring more readily in this environment, or the detector's 5-minute detection threshold plus restart/recovery time doesn't leave enough margin inside the test's 10-minute timeout. No PR diff was supplied for this run, so I can't assess relatedness to a specific code change beyond what's in `master` already.","time":{"start":1793573870000,"stop":1793575851530,"duration":1981530}},{"uid":"67248d2de61965f5","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/4/#testresult/67248d2de61965f5","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793485364000,"stop":1793486651400,"duration":1287400}},{"uid":"a050341117a9d423","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/3/#testresult/a050341117a9d423","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793398896000,"stop":1793399343360,"duration":447360}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"7f7a3bf624a9f363.json","parameterValues":[]}